<title>USA: Georgia-Pacific Corp Q3 after gain.</title>
<headline>Georgia-Pacific Corp Q3 after gain.</headline>
<dateline>ATLANTA 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Dollar amounts, except per share, in millions)</p>
<p>						   1996		  1995</p>
<p> NET SALES				    3,446		 3,705</p>
<p> Net income					99		   324</p>
<p>Per share:</p>
<p> Net income				    1.09		  3.57</p>
<p> Average shares outstanding		90.6		  90.7</p>
<p>NINE MONTHS</p>
<p> NET SALES					9,814	    10,882</p>
<p> Income before extraordinary item	   159		 821</p>
<p> Extraordinary item, net of tax	     (5)		 ---</p>
<p> Net income					 154		 821</p>
<p>Per share:</p>
<p> Income before extraordinary item	  1.75		9.12</p>
<p> Extraordinary item, net of tax	   (.05)		 ---</p>
<p> Net income					1.70		9.12</p>
<p> Average shares outstanding		  90.5		90.0</p>
<p>NOTES: 1996 Q3 includes pretax income of $78 million ($48 million after taxes). The sale of two gypsum wallboard production facilities generated a pretax gain of $41 million, equal to $25 million, or $0.28/shr, after taxes. The remaining gain of $37 million, equal to $23 million, or $0.25/shr, after taxes, primarily related to settlement of pension obligations from the implementation of the company's voluntary early retirement program.</p>
<p>1996 Q2 net includes other pretax expense of $74 million primarily from voluntary early retirement program.</p>
<p>1996 nine months extraordinary item resulted from call of about $150 million of debt during Q2.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
